{"assets":["/statement-assets/5dc77d133dd6535f8337ed0e3fbde0e3d114d0a0a4f4ddb40972249b1c09be0e.png","/statement-assets/0d3541ed0b2ed8312ffb1b979a33ac4d741b934ec1531ef313d56585a6134fc9.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1748","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. The Ultimate Square"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have $$$n$$$ rectangular wooden blocks, which are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. The $$$i$$$-th block is $$$1$$$ unit high and $$$\\lceil \\frac{i}{2} \\rceil$$$ units long."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here, $$$\\lceil \\frac{x}{2} \\rceil$$$ denotes the result of division of $$$x$$$ by $$$2$$$, rounded "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"up"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, $$$\\lceil \\frac{4}{2} \\rceil = 2$$$ and $$$\\lceil \\frac{5}{2} \\rceil = \\lceil 2.5 \\rceil = 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$n=5$$$, then the blocks have the following sizes: $$$1 \\times 1$$$, $$$1 \\times 1$$$, $$$1 \\times 2$$$, $$$1 \\times 2$$$, $$$1 \\times 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5dc77d133dd6535f8337ed0e3fbde0e3d114d0a0a4f4ddb40972249b1c09be0e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The available blocks for $$$n=5$$$"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the maximum possible side length of a square you can create using these blocks, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"without rotating any of them"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that you don't have to use all of the blocks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0d3541ed0b2ed8312ffb1b979a33ac4d741b934ec1531ef313d56585a6134fc9.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the ways to create $$$3 \\times 3$$$ square using blocks $$$1$$$ through $$$5$$$"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^9$$$) — the number of blocks."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print one integer — the maximum possible side length of a square you can create."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2\n5\n197654321\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n3\n98827161\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, you can create a $$$1 \\times 1$$$ square using only one of the blocks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, one of the possible ways to create a $$$3 \\times 3$$$ square is shown in the statement. It is impossible to create a $$$4 \\times 4$$$ or larger square, so the answer is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1748A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1748/problem/A"}